---
import '../styles/global.css';
import Head from '../layouts/Head.astro'
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Navigation from '../components/Navigation.astro';
import PortfolioLayout from '../layouts/PortfolioLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<html lang="en">
	<Head title="Portfolio"/>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<div class="page">
            <Navigation />
			<div class="content" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
				<h1>Portfolio</h1>
                <p>Hello, I'm Jack, a games programmer from the North-East of England, currently studying Games Development at Teeside University.</p>
			</div>
            <PortfolioLayout project="JustSpirit.dev" date="02/10/'26" image="JSDev.png" alt="">
                <p class="desc">
                    The very website you are reading this on. Planned to include all sorts such as: a gallery; fiction writing; blog posts; and a forum...?
                </p>
                <div class="skills">
					Astro<br>
					HTML<br>
					CSS<br>
                </div>
                <div slot="expand">
                    JustSpirit.dev is my custom website built to house whatever I wish. The website has been made using Astro, hosted on GitHub, protected by Cloudflare with the domain provided via Hostinger. It's constantly expanding as I work on adding new things.
                </div>
            </PortfolioLayout>
            <PortfolioLayout project="Skill Creation System" date="06/01/'26" image="SCS.png" alt="">
                <p class="desc">
                    The Skill Creation System is a highly modular Unity Plugin intended to be all encompassing and able to let a designer create any "skill", "spell" or "ability" with minimal setup.
                </p>
                <div class="skills">
					Unity 6<br>
					C#<br>
					Plugin Dev<br>
                </div>
                <div slot="expand">
                    The Skill Creation System (SCS) was a highly interconnected and malleable Unity 6 plugin designed with the intention to let designers build complicated skills, spells and abilities without the need for them to modify code. The system is split into distinct sections around the type of ability they are such as melee or ranged as well as full support for attaching custom scripts.<br/><br/>
                    <a href="https://github.com/ImJustSpirit/Grandeur/tree/main/Skill%20Creation%20System"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" fill="currentColor" class="bi bi-github" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8c0 3.54 2.29 6.53 5.47 7.59.4.07.55-.17.55-.38 0-.19-.01-.82-.01-1.49-2.01.37-2.53-.49-2.69-.94-.09-.23-.48-.94-.82-1.13-.28-.15-.68-.52-.01-.53.63-.01 1.08.58 1.23.82.72 1.21 1.87.87 2.33.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82.64-.18 1.32-.27 2-.27s1.36.09 2 .27c1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48 0 1.07-.01 1.93-.01 2.2 0 .21.15.46.55.38A8.01 8.01 0 0 0 16 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8"/></svg></a>
                </div>
            </PortfolioLayout>
            <PortfolioLayout project="My Day Out :)" date="26/10/'25" image="MyDayOut.png" alt="">
                <p class="desc">
                    Created for DrinkDevs 2025, our team of three took theme of "False Advertising" and made a crayon drawn platformer which takes a gory turn.
                </p>
                <div class="skills">
					Team Lead<br>
					Unity '22<br>
					C#<br>
                    Game Jam
                </div>
                <div slot="expand">
                    There is a lot of directions you can take the theme of false advertising, many great ones were displayed at the reward ceremony of the event. Our idea was taking the cutesy, naive drawings of a child and turning them into a gory run and gun platformer ending with you fighting the sun.<br/><br/>
                    <a href="https://infallinteractive.itch.io/my-day-out"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" fill="currentColor" class="bi bi-shop-window" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M2.97 1.35A1 1 0 0 1 3.73 1h8.54a1 1 0 0 1 .76.35l2.609 3.044A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 16 5.37v.255a2.375 2.375 0 0 1-4.25 1.458A2.37 2.37 0 0 1 9.875 8 2.37 2.37 0 0 1 8 7.083 2.37 2.37 0 0 1 6.125 8a2.37 2.37 0 0 1-1.875-.917A2.375 2.375 0 0 1 0 5.625V5.37a1.5 1.5 0 0 1 .361-.976zm1.78 4.275a1.375 1.375 0 0 0 2.75 0 .5.5 0 0 1 1 0 1.375 1.375 0 0 0 2.75 0 .5.5 0 0 1 1 0 1.375 1.375 0 1 0 2.75 0V5.37a.5.5 0 0 0-.12-.325L12.27 2H3.73L1.12 5.045A.5.5 0 0 0 1 5.37v.255a1.375 1.375 0 0 0 2.75 0 .5.5 0 0 1 1 0M1.5 8.5A.5.5 0 0 1 2 9v6h12V9a.5.5 0 0 1 1 0v6h.5a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1H.5a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1H1V9a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5m2 .5a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5V13h8V9.5a.5.5 0 0 1 1 0V13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V9.5a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5"/></svg></a>
                </div>
            </PortfolioLayout>
            <PortfolioLayout project="Ouroboros Engine" date="03/08/'25" image="OuroborosEngine.png" alt="">
                <p class="desc">
                    Made for the GMTK Game Jam 2025 as a team of three, Ouroboros Engine took the theme of "Loop" and put you in a train tower-defence game.
                </p>
                <div class="skills">
					Team Lead<br>
					Unity '22<br>
					C#<br>
                    Game Jam
                </div>
                <div slot="expand">
                    When it came to figuring out what to do with the theme of "Looping", we were stuck for a good few hours. Eventually though, we landed on our star idea. A tower defence game where you not only build on the defence point itself, but it also moves through different terrain as the game increasingly scales up in difficulty, with even bosses being able to spawn.<br/><br/>
                    <a href="https://infallinteractive.itch.io/ouroboros-engine"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" fill="currentColor" class="bi bi-shop-window" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M2.97 1.35A1 1 0 0 1 3.73 1h8.54a1 1 0 0 1 .76.35l2.609 3.044A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 16 5.37v.255a2.375 2.375 0 0 1-4.25 1.458A2.37 2.37 0 0 1 9.875 8 2.37 2.37 0 0 1 8 7.083 2.37 2.37 0 0 1 6.125 8a2.37 2.37 0 0 1-1.875-.917A2.375 2.375 0 0 1 0 5.625V5.37a1.5 1.5 0 0 1 .361-.976zm1.78 4.275a1.375 1.375 0 0 0 2.75 0 .5.5 0 0 1 1 0 1.375 1.375 0 0 0 2.75 0 .5.5 0 0 1 1 0 1.375 1.375 0 1 0 2.75 0V5.37a.5.5 0 0 0-.12-.325L12.27 2H3.73L1.12 5.045A.5.5 0 0 0 1 5.37v.255a1.375 1.375 0 0 0 2.75 0 .5.5 0 0 1 1 0M1.5 8.5A.5.5 0 0 1 2 9v6h12V9a.5.5 0 0 1 1 0v6h.5a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1H.5a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1H1V9a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5m2 .5a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5V13h8V9.5a.5.5 0 0 1 1 0V13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V9.5a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5"/></svg></a>
                </div>
            </PortfolioLayout>
            <PortfolioLayout project="Dungeon Merchant" date="11/12/'23" image="DungeonMerchant.png" alt="">
                <p class="desc">
                    Dungeon Merchant is a game concept based around diving into a dungeon to retrieve loot to the pawn off to the masses.
                </p>
                <div class="skills">
					Game Design<br>
					Level Design<br>
					World Design<br>
                </div>
                <div slot="expand">
                    Dungeon Merchant was a project I worked on all the way back in my college days where we had to design a game concept in a tight timeframe. The importance of this is furthering the ability to quicker recognise important game details and expand on them without letting scope creep up.
                </div>
            </PortfolioLayout>
		</div>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
